This product includes software developed by Google LLC and contributors
(gemini-cli-extensions/workspace, Apache-2.0), vendored under src/vendored/ (services + utils).

`scripts/sync-upstream.mjs` pulls a newer upstream revision over the vendored tree. It READS THE
LISTS BELOW to decide what it may overwrite, so the lists are the contract, not documentation of it:
edit them in the same commit that adds, forks or unforks a file. Every non-test file under
src/vendored/ is listed in exactly one section (a test enforces it). The script refuses to run if a
list is unparseable or names a file that is not on disk -- an empty list would otherwise read as
"nothing is protected" and overwrite every fork in silence.

`vitest.config.ts` reads the same lists: forked files and the files that are ours (the last two
sections) count toward the 95% coverage gate; byte-identical files do not, since every sync
overwrites them.

